  "notes": "Composed of {滑|かっ} (slide/glide) and {走|そう} (run). The word covers any smooth sliding movement along a surface, but is most strongly associated with aircraft and skiing.\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {滑走路|かっそうろ}: runway\n- {滑走|かっそう}する: to glide, to taxi\n- {滑走|かっそう}{距離|きょり}: gliding/taxiing distance\n- {滑走|かっそう}{速度|そくど}: taxiing speed\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {滑|すべ}る: to slide/slip — the everyday verb for sliding; {滑走|かっそう} is more formal and implies sustained, purposeful movement\n- {走行|そうこう}: running/traveling — movement of vehicles on roads, not gliding\n- {離陸|りりく}: takeoff — the act of leaving the ground, which follows {滑走|かっそう}",
